      "date": "2026-07-27 15:50:43.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(2 comments)\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nMostly good, a couple of comments inline. The premise checks out: nothing under lustre/utils/, lnet/utils/ or lustre/tests/ issues this ioctl, and OBD_IOC_GETDEVICE already reports each device's UUID, so userspace can resolve a UUID from `lctl dl` output. The main question is whether the interface should go through the tree's existing deprecation path first rather than being deleted in one step.",
